module gunbc.githooks.githooks_pre_push_frontier

// THE PRE-PUSH CONCAT BODY ON THE CLOSURE'S FRONTIER. This registers the residual in the
// production roster fold — gunbc.census_closure_frontier.census_closure_frontier_rows() — so
// the row is read by something other than tests: gunbc.dissolution_census.dissolution_census_verdict()
// and dissolution_census_holds() resolve every registered row's trigger against the live
// declaration index and refuse what they cannot decide, and frontier_rows_well_formed() checks
// every row's shape. That is the same route that carries every other dissolution in the closure
// (the extdeps.tools.sha256sum shell-only row is the closest sibling: an unbound capability
// trigger over a foreign-executor body). The trigger row itself lives once, in
// gunbc.githooks.githooks_pre_push_emit (githooks_pre_push_emit_concat_body_dissolution), next
// to the body it names; this module is its registration, not a second statement of it.
//
// WHY THE BODY IS A RESIDUAL AT ALL. expected_githooks_pre_push_sh assembles the committed
// .githooks/pre-push by concatenation; the cutover to emission through v2.workflow.bash_emit is
// blocked on the emitter's vocabulary, not on wiring — v2.workflow.bash_emit renders only the
// statement kinds gunbc.languages.bash spells, and the hook's lines use forms that module does
// not model (the #!/usr/bin/env shebang line, comment lines, 'set -euo pipefail' — the renderer
// spells 'set -e' only —, the while-read loop, case/esac, [[ ]] tests, $(( )) arithmetic, and
// >&2 fd redirection; with-redir is file-only and while/case are ingest-recognized-unmodeled in
// gunbc.languages.bash_command_fold). Emitting those forms through concat is exactly the
// refusal-flattening DESIGN §5 forbids. The hook STAYS shell permanently — a git hook is one of
// the foreign executors DESIGN's shell-to-intent routing names (GHA run:, cron, git hooks): no
// gunbc runtime is present at push time (census §1.A category (a),
// docs/plans/shell-to-dag-residual-census-and-arc-completion.md). The cutover changes who
// assembles the bytes, never the language.
//
// PROVENANCE (review 45175): the hook-emit family trigger was once tracked only on the
// githooks_pre_commit_emit sibling and the pre-push half inherited it implicitly — the
// implicit-marker shape the medium gate asks not to rely on. The row's own carrier states it
// on this surface; the registered Scaffold remains the single authority in
// gunbc.local_tidy_spec (githooks_pre_push_emit_scaffold, binding expected_githooks_pre_push_sh
// with dissolves_to RealizationDispatch). A Scaffold carries no trigger, so no second statement
// of the dissolution exists: mechanism+bind in the Scaffold, reason+trigger here.

import gunbc.githooks.githooks_pre_push_emit { githooks_pre_push_emit_concat_body_dissolution }

